summary:
- topic: Celebrations of Student Achievement
  text: The meeting began by celebrating the AA State Champion Girls Basketball Team
    with a video, certificates, and remarks from the coach, captains, and board members.
    The board also recognized three high school students—Elsa Hendrickson, Pepper
    Hinman, and Leo Graphos—for their winning submissions in the Scholastic Art Awards.
- topic: Student Representative Report
  text: Student Representative Eliot Wertheimer reported on numerous school activities,
    including successful Black History Month celebrations across the district, a Kaler
    Elementary family engagement night, the high school drama club's participation
    in the One Act festival, and a wrap-up of the winter athletics season.
- topic: 'FY26 Budget Presentation: Context and Drivers'
  text: Superintendent Matheney presented the proposed FY26 budget, explaining the
    difficult financial context. Key drivers for a potential $9 million budget increase
    include declining enrollment, the loss of COVID-era and other carryover funds,
    contractual salary increases, rising benefits costs, and inflation.
- topic: 'FY26 Budget Presentation: Proposed Reductions'
  text: To close the budget gap, the superintendent proposed a $72.9M budget, representing
    a 5.98% increase. This includes eliminating approximately 20 positions across
    the district, including the Director of Curriculum, teachers (ESOL, SEL, Social
    Studies), and Ed Techs. The plan also involves reorganizing curriculum leadership
    and changing elementary library time to a 'special' to cover teacher prep time
    lost from SEL classes.
- topic: Public Comment on Budget Cuts
  text: An extensive public comment period featured dozens of teachers, parents, and
    students speaking passionately against the proposed cuts. Common themes included
    a perceived lack of transparency and union involvement in the budget process,
    the "callous" nature of the email layoff notifications, and strong opposition
    to cutting positions in social-emotional learning (SEL), music, social studies,
    special education, and multilingual learner (ESOL) support.
- topic: Policy and Program Approvals
  text: The board unanimously approved the consent agenda and held second readings
    to approve policies on copyright compliance and field trips. They also unanimously
    approved the expansion of the pilot Pre-Kindergarten Program through a public-private
    partnership that comes at no cost to taxpayers.
